+# `evidence/` — the manuscript evidence root
+
+**What this is.** The compact, versioned set of archived result files, figures
+and tables that the manuscript reads.  A clean checkout of this repository can
+rebuild every generated figure and table, re-read every machine-checked claim
+value and produce every build from this directory alone — no access to the
+experiment host's raw-data filesystem is required.
+
+**What this is not.** It is not the experiment archive.  The experiment
+repository `noise-weighted-subspace-reconstruction` remains the source of
+record for runners, configurations, logs and complete run trees.  This
+directory is a declared *export* of that record: every file carries a SHA-256
+in `MANIFEST.json`, and `scripts/materialize_evidence.py` regenerates the
+export and reports any divergence.
+
+## History
+
+Until 11 September 2026 the same files lived in `transfer_paper/`, a bundle
+duplicated byte-for-byte in both repositories with no mechanism keeping the two
+copies in step — `OPEN_ISSUES.md` #10 recorded that as a standing risk.  MS
+`bf7d5f6` removed the manuscript's copy; the LaTeX, the claim validator, the
+figure generators, the packaging list and the bundle verifier still pointed at
+it, so the build and the evidence checks broke.  This directory completes that
+migration:
+
+| before | after |
+|---|---|
+| `transfer_paper/data/…`, `transfer_paper/figures/…` | `evidence/data/…`, `evidence/figures/…` |
+| `transfer_paper/BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json` | `evidence/MANIFEST.json` (schema `paper1-evidence-manifest/1`) |
+| `transfer_paper/scripts/verify_bundle.py` | `scripts/verify_evidence.py` |
+| hardcoded `transfer_paper/` in five tools | `scripts/evidence_root.py`: `--evidence-root`, `$PAPER1_EVIDENCE_ROOT`, else `<repo>/evidence` |
+| bundle refreshed by hand | `scripts/materialize_evidence.py` (`--source` or `--from-git`) |
+
+The historical bundle documents — including the 327-entry
+`BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json` that the recovered bytes were checked against — are kept
+verbatim under `archive/transfer_paper_docs/`.
+
+## Recovery and integrity
+
+The bytes here were recovered from this repository's own history at MS
+`c826ef6`, the commit immediately before the removal, and checked against the
+recorded `BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json`: **327 of 327 listed entries matched** on
+SHA-256 and byte count, with no missing file and no mismatch.  The only
+`--require-complete` failures in that historical manifest were the 24 Part II
+files added on 11 September 2026 that had never been listed; all 24 are listed
+in `MANIFEST.json` now.
+
+Reproduce either check:
+
+```bash
+python3 scripts/materialize_evidence.py --from-git c826ef6      # rebuild
+python3 scripts/materialize_evidence.py --from-git c826ef6 --check
+python3 scripts/verify_evidence.py --require-complete
+python3 scripts/verify_evidence.py --require-complete \
+    --compare <EXP>/transfer_paper          # against the experiment copy
+```
+
+## Contents and policy
+
+251 files, 20.6 MB: `data/` 20.1 MB, `figures/` 0.47 MB, `tables/` 0.02 MB,
+plus `MANUSCRIPT_EVIDENCE_MAP.md`.  The policy is recorded in
+`MANIFEST.json → policy` and applied by `materialize_evidence.py`:
+
+* **`data/`** — everything, except the prefix below.
+* **`figures/`** — vector `.pdf` (plus the two `.tex`/`.md` companions) only.
+  The thirteen `.png` twins were preview artefacts for the notebooks and are
+  not included; the manuscript includes the PDFs.
+* **`tables/`** — everything.
+* **Excluded, retained in EXP:** `data/gwosc/runs/` — 66 files, 5.16 MB, three
+  superseded GWOSC run directories.  `data/gwosc/current/` *is* the registered
+  run (`20260622T175125Z_b169c1f595a4`) that claim row 11 cites, and it is
+  exported.  Every excluded path is listed with its SHA-256 and byte count
+  under `MANIFEST.json → excluded_retained_in_exp`, so its absence is a
+  checkable decision: `verify_evidence.py` fails if such a path reappears
+  unlisted, and the bytes are recoverable from `<EXP>/transfer_paper/` or from
+  MS `c826ef6`.
+* **Filtered by tree/suffix policy:** 38 paths — the `.png` twins, the five
+  rendering notebooks and the ten bundle-maintenance scripts, all listed under
+  `MANIFEST.json → filtered_by_policy`.
+* **Owned by a manuscript script, not by the historical bundle:** the four
+  paths in `MANIFEST.json → policy.regenerated_paths`.  `materialize_evidence.py`
+  hashes them but never overwrites them; each manifest entry names its
+  `produced_by`.
+
+## Recorded provenance gaps
+
+These are gaps in the *origin record*.  They are separate from file integrity:
+every file in this directory verifies against `MANIFEST.json`.
+
+**(G1) The Part II run tree is not on the experiment host.**
+`evidence/data/paper1/mlst_2026-09-11/{t19,t19_sminus_v2,t20,t21}` are copies
+of `EXP:results/mlst_2026-09-11/…` at EXP `ea076ff`, branch
+`mlst/exp-phase-20260911`.  Neither that commit nor that branch exists in the
+synchronized experiment repository, whose MLST branch ends at
+`mlst/exp-phase-20260910` (through T15); the runs were executed on the local
+phase host.  Consequence: the copies here are the only accessible instance.
+Each carries the source tree's own `RESULTS_SHA256`, and those verify, so the
+files are intact and self-consistent; what cannot be re-derived here is the
+run tree they came from.  The claim table therefore cites the
+`MS:evidence/…` paths, which resolve, and names `EXP:results/mlst_2026-09-11/`
+as the origin in prose.  *To close:* copy or bundle EXP
+`mlst/exp-phase-20260911` from the local phase host.
+
+**(G2) Execution revision of the September 2026 Paper-1 runs.**  Pre-existing,
+recorded in `CLAIM_EVIDENCE_TABLE.md` and `OPEN_ISSUES.md`: P1-E0/E2/E4b/E6/E9/
+E11/E12 ran at EXP `3026d25` with a dirty tree, so the archived JSONs carry no
+`git_commit` and the first committed revision (`00b5aee`) is not the execution
+revision.  Unchanged by this migration; not closable retrospectively.
+
+**(Closed, 11 September 2026) Transcribed Fig. 10 inputs.**  The three
+`tidmad_heldout_*_2026-09-10.csv` files were transcribed from the printed
+phase report because the T10–T12 archive was believed unreachable.  The archive
+was found on the execution host at `results/mlst_2026-09-10/`, verified against
+its `RESULTS_SHA256`, and the CSVs are now exported from it at full precision
+by `scripts/export_tidmad_heldout.py`.  See
+`data/paper1/mlst_2026-09-11/README.md` for the numerical consequences.
