+# Part II local-phase archives (T19, T20, T21), copied 2026-09-11
+
+Byte-exact copies of the frozen result archives under
+`noise-weighted-subspace-reconstruction/results/mlst_2026-09-11/` at EXP commit
+`ea076ff` (branch `mlst/exp-phase-20260911`).  Each directory carries the
+`RESULTS_SHA256` manifest of the source tree; verify with
+`sha256sum -c RESULTS_SHA256` inside the directory.  Only the files the
+paper-facing figures read are copied (summaries, seed-level rows, manifests).
+
+These are inputs to `figures_src/make_part2_figures.py`; never edit by hand.
+
+**Recorded provenance gap (11 September 2026).**  The originating EXP tree
+`results/mlst_2026-09-11/` and the branch `mlst/exp-phase-20260911` were
+produced on the local execution host and are *not* present in the synchronized
+experiment repository on the run host, whose MLST branch ends at
+`mlst/exp-phase-20260910` (T10–T15).  The copies here are therefore the only
+accessible instance of those results.  Their own `RESULTS_SHA256` manifests
+verify, so file integrity is established; the originating run tree is not
+re-derivable here.  See `evidence/PROVENANCE.md`, gap (G1).
+
+## TIDMAD held-out inputs — transcription replaced, 11 September 2026
+
+`tidmad_heldout_perfile_2026-09-10.csv`,
+`tidmad_heldout_combined_2026-09-10.csv` and
+`tidmad_heldout_rmse_by_method_2026-09-10.csv` were originally *transcribed*
+from the printed tables of `reviews/2026-09-10-experiment-phase-report.md`
+(§4.5 final test, §4.6 RMSE by method), at two significant figures and with
+some interval endpoints left blank, because the T10–T12 run archive had been
+produced on the execution host and was not reachable from the machine that
+built the figures.
+
+The archive **was** located on the execution host on 11 September 2026 at
+`results/mlst_2026-09-10/` (stage outputs `T10_tidmad_validation_v1/t10_validation.json`
+and `T10_tidmad_final_test_v1/t10_final-test.json`, both verifying against
+their `RESULTS_SHA256`).  The three files are now written by
+
+```
+python3 scripts/export_tidmad_heldout.py --results <EXP>/results/mlst_2026-09-10
+```
+
+at full double precision, with two added columns — `bootstrap_sd_zero_empca`
+and `bootstrap_sd_calmean_empca` — and `in_combined_estimate`.  Every value
+that the transcription carried agrees with the archive at the transcribed
+precision; nothing was re-run and no estimand changed.  What the replacement
+fixes is downstream: the post-hoc sensitivity table in
+`generated/tables/tidmad_heldout_sensitivity.md` previously had to infer each
+file's bootstrap sd from rounded interval endpoints, which reproduced the
+archived precision-weighted estimate as +2.406e−06 (Q = 359.4) instead of the
+archived +1.5845e−05 (Q = 328.33).  With the archived standard deviations the
+recomputation now reproduces θ_IV and Q exactly.  The manuscript's post-hoc
+DerSimonian–Laird interval moves from [+2.0e−03, +1.1e−02] to
+[+1.9e−03, +1.1e−02]; the equal-file mean, all three verdicts and the primary
+estimand are unchanged.
